Hi,

I use the a syba SY-PEX40033 , the card has 2 e-sata 3 ports and
supports port multiplexing (PMP) of 4 drives per port, for a total of
8 drives.  It supports FBS / CBS.

It seems to have some problems, especially when I'm running a java
program (vuze) and it's installation folder is on the raidz volume the
drives on the card consist of.  Funny enough high IO alone doesn't
seem to trigger issues so much (say from filesystem checks).   The
lockup just affects the filesystem and drives, so the computer isn't
completely hung up.  Thus I'm able to get in some debugging if
necessary and log collection.

I'm attaching my syslog showing the hangup.  You can see some failed
ata commands and other errors.

I've also had a run where I disabled NCQ by setting device/queue_depth
to 1 for each drive.  It didn't seem to have any effect, the same
types of errors were in both logs.

These errors occurred on 3.7.2, the first kernel I started using the card with.

-Jason

